{"kind":"request","text":"P0: bound every resident HTTP call and shutdown path. The MCP adapter currently inherits a background context and an HTTP client without a timeout, so a resident that accepts a connection and stops responding can hang a tool call or process shutdown indefinitely. Add one explicit end-to-end deadline policy, preserve caller cancellation, distinguish timeout errors, bound response-body handling as appropriate, and prove stalled request and stalled shutdown behavior without weakening redirect or repository-routing checks.","body":{"branch":"request/resident-call-deadlines","conditions":"All resident HTTP request construction and client paths use bounded contexts/timeouts rather than context.Background plus an unbounded client; graceful shutdown has an independent bounded deadline; tests deterministically cover a resident that accepts but never responds and a shutdown that stalls, asserting bounded return and useful errors; redirect refusal, repository routing, local fallback, and existing two-second whoami behavior remain correct; full gates and independent exact-head review pass.","priority":"P0","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}